# Data Layer & Repositories

## Interfaces
- ✅ Repository interfaces live in `domain/`
- ✅ Implementations live in `data/`
- ✅ Expose repos via providers returning interfaces (e.g. `Provider<AuthRepository>`), constructed with shared dependencies like `dioProvider`

## Mapping
- ✅ Repository returns domain entities/value objects only
- ✅ Map exceptions to `Failure` (see `lib/shared/errors/failure.dart`); do not leak Dio exceptions beyond data layer (use `DioFailureMapper`)

## Caching
- ✅ If caching exists, document:
  - TTL
  - invalidation
  - stale-while-revalidate behavior

## Testability
- ✅ Repositories are mockable (depend on interfaces)
- ✅ API clients and local sources are separated for unit tests

## NEVER
- ❌ Return DTOs to presentation
- ❌ Throw Dio exceptions beyond data layer
